				<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>According to <a href="http://www.forbes.com/sites/dinagachman/2015/02/09/wheres-beyonce-top-five-2015-grammy-moments-from-tivo/" target="_blank">Forbes</a>, the most-watched moment of last Grammy night was <strong>Madonna</strong> singing <strong>Living For Love</strong> for the first time on a tv show!</p>
<blockquote><p>1. Madonna’s performance of “Living for Love” came in at number one. The woman will probably still be rocking fishnet stockings and corsets on stage when she’s 75 years old – and that’s why we love her. Her matador number might not have been the best performance of her career (or of last night’s Grammys) but she’s Madonna. It’s not like she needs to prove herself anymore. She appears on a stage, we watch.</p></blockquote>
