<p><em>Bow down, haters, <strong>Madonna</strong> has reclaimed her throne as the eternal <strong>Queen of Pop</strong> (not to imply she ever relinquished it) with her stirring performance of the anthemic “Living for Love” at the 2015 Grammy Awards Sunday evening. After flashing her unbelievably-toned ass</a> on the red carpet, the 56-year-old entertainer donned a red matador-themed outfit backed by dancers sporting Maleficent-style horned headpieces to perform the first single, a certain club hit with a sing-along chorus, from her upcoming Rebel Heart album. Madonna and company had the celeb-filled crowd (we see you, Taylor Swift!) on their feet, clapping and dancing along.</em><br />
Watch her Majesty perform below and check out her official video <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=u9h7Teiyvc8" target="_blank">here</a>.</p>
